---
description: Challenge actual inferred readings and repair without rebuilding a preferred corpus.
args:
  request: LinguisticRequest
  source: CorpusSource
  graph: EvidenceGraph
  grammar: GrammarReport
  translations: TranslationReport
  patch: PatchProposal
returns: LinguisticReport
---
1. Inventory actual original source clauses and actual returned stage provenance. Separate unused contextual evidence from a missing decisive premise; document count alone does not establish connected semantic coverage.
2. Check original domain integrity, exact quote/span reconstruction and actual candidate/evidence accounting. These exact checks validate the actual certificate, not whether a suffix means agent or topic.
3. For every actual target reading call challengeReading(reading, source, graph, grammar). Retain the actual grounded/contradicted/unresolved challenge beside that exact reading.
4. Call challengePatch(patch, source, graph, grammar, translations). Preserve its actual findings instead of replacing the edit with a newly authored ideal gloss.
5. Trace actual grammar attempts and translation readings back to their real scoped boundary/role/compatibility/context child results. Missing actual contribution is unresolved execution evidence, not a new candidate contradiction.
6. Ensure the actual report distinguishes finite surviving alternatives, failed source interpretation and unsupported repair authority. An exact-valid output can still require independent semantic judgment.
7. Return LinguisticReport containing actual source, graph, grammar, translations, patch, all actual reading challenges, original sourceCoverage and unresolved findings. No source-only certificate grants live qualification or training admission.
